Z||000007||Nashco||10-30-2001||12:24 PM||||GM, excitement?  It seems GM and Ford are great at making sweet prototypes, horrible at realizing them.  They love to show off the hot stuff they have in the company, while it's actually more like teasing than showing off.  That's what I think, anyway.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||Patrick's Dad||10-30-2001||09:42 PM||||&lt;quote&gt;GM, excitement? It seems GM and Ford are great at making sweet prototypes, horrible at realizing them. They love to show off the hot stuff they have in the company, while it's actually more like teasing than showing off. That's what I think, anyway.&lt;/quote&gt;<P>Right now, I am swinging back towards hope for the General. The (Ponti) Vibe looks like a neat car (and also looks like a Sunfire replacement) that will offer a 1.8 liter four with 5 speed and AWD for not a lot of bucks, and a supercharger (possibly) to bolt on within a year or so. The (Chevy) SSR will get an aluminum 5.3l V8, and Caddy is rolling out a performance division, a la BMW M's, that may see the CTS with the LS1/6sp that is available in Europe. Could Lutz already be working his magic?||||reg||1
Z||000009||Shaun41178||10-30-2001||11:18 PM||||GM isn't going to do squat with that car.  Remember the Cavalier Z24 Moab?  190 hp 4 banger?  Had bigger cams, header and TB or something and some chip tuning.  They said there was a really good chance that that car might come out.  And it never did.  No surprise there.  Domestic manufacturers dont' try and compete with the import market.  They just talk about doing it.  GM is talk.  Ford is the only one doing something about it with there little ZX2 or whatever it is and it really isnt' doing all so well when it can only muster a mid 16 qtr.<P>You can forget it.<P>What I like is the Corvette engine in the Grand Prix with AWD from a aztec.  Now that is a cool combo.  That won't ever happen either but shows that it can be done I guess.  Would be nice to have.  380 hp AWD would be sweet.  hold on tight<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Mach10||10-30-2001||11:26 PM||||<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>From the Cadaver</B><BR>Front-wheel drive coupe <BR>220 hp modified Ecotec 2.2-liter four-cylinder engine <BR>Five-speed manual transmission <BR>**Custom designed body kit that includes unique front and rear fascias, body side moldings, hood with ram air scoops, rear spoiler and taillamps**<BR>Nippon Stealth Gray exterior paint <BR>Custom interior with black and aluminum accents <BR>**Racing Hart M-5 three-piece 19 x 8-inch wheels and Toyo Proxes FZ-4 tires**<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I'm sorry, 19" rims on a CAVALIER??! Oh, the HUMANITY!<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>From the Sunfire:</B><BR>2.4-liter supercharged four-cylinder engine <BR>Polished aluminum engine components with semi-gloss finish on painted components <BR>**Five-inch diameter dual exhaust outlets integrated into rear fascia**<BR>Lowered ride-height <BR>18-inch high-gloss wheels <BR>Four-wheel performance disc brakes with **painted brake calipers**<BR>**New front fascia with Xenon fog lamps**<BR>**Front air dam**<BR>**New rear fascia**<BR>**Three-piece rear deck spoiler with articulating center wing and integrated CHMSL**<BR>Body-color fender flares <BR>**Functional hood vents with grille screens**<BR>Outside rear view mirrors housings with **incorporated turn signals/strobe lamps** <BR>**Sport driver and passenger seats**<BR>**Upgraded seatbelt/harness**<BR>Leather-wrapped sport steering wheel <BR>**Aluminum shift knob and parking brake**<BR>*****Fire extinguisher******<BR>DVD visor screens, video camera and remote camera lens <BR>Center-mounted storage bracket for video system remote control <BR>Upgraded sound components with high-output XM Radio system <BR>**Metal floor mats**<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Jebus Cripes.... these things had better be FAST... These things just SCREAM "rice"||||reg||13
Z||000011||Nashco||10-31-2001||03:08 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Shaun41178:<BR><B>GM isn't going to do squat with that car.  Remember the Cavalier Z24 Moab?  190 hp 4 banger?  Had bigger cams, header and TB or something and some chip tuning.  They said there was a really good chance that that car might come out.  And it never did.  No surprise there.  Domestic manufacturers dont' try and compete with the import market.  They just talk about doing it.  GM is talk.  Ford is the only one doing something about it with there little ZX2 or whatever it is and it really isnt' doing all so well when it can only muster a mid 16 qtr.<P>You can forget it.<P>What I like is the Corvette engine in the Grand Prix with AWD from a aztec.  Now that is a cool combo.  That won't ever happen either but shows that it can be done I guess.  Would be nice to have.  380 hp AWD would be sweet.  hold on tight</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I saw that Grand Prix in person at Detroit, and man oh man, what a beautiful concept.  Like I said, nice to see what COULD be, thanks for the tease GM.  If something like this ever becomes a reality, I will be the first to say I guessed wrong.  I just don't see it happening.  Although this would probably be the best selling AWD performance car in America a few years after release, GM doesn't have what it takes to get past the bean counters that don't like cars.  Humph..I guess I can always buy an import with some guts...but then again, I want the JAPANESE spec versions, so I still think I'm getting jipped! LOL..<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<BR>||||reg||1
