Z||000014||Pontiaddict||11-02-2001||12:53 AM||||You guys are missing the big picture. Both those motors would make nice Fiero engine swaps. I thought the new Ecotec was a 2.3 liter though. Oh well.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Red2m4||11-02-2001||01:49 PM||||say what you will about mopars...but chrysler is the only american car company that will actually produce something that resembles their concepts.  Ex.  The viper, the prowler and the pt cruiser.  (Yes, I'm ignoring the ugly-as-sin jeep liberty.) Even their trucks were cutting edge as far as styling was concerned.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Fformula88||11-02-2001||02:21 PM||||The Vibe might look lijke an "interesting" car, but GM has already missed the boat with the thing!  <P>1) They are essentially replacing the Firebird with it.  Take away a blazign fast musclecar and replace it with a *cough* sport wagon!  <P>2) There one chance to make something of the Vibe was to use the 180 HP engine with the AWD system, but they are NOT.  The AWD is going to be available with the 140 HP engine only.<P>3) Its not a GM car in my book.  It has a Toyota drivetrain, is built in a Toyota plant, and is based on the new Toyota Matrix.  Even if it is a fairly exciting new GM car, to say its GM isn't exactly true.  Sporty hybrid vehicles have not faired too well in the market either (Plymouth Lazer version of the Mitsu Eclipse, and the Ford Probe/Mazda MX-6 come readily to mind).<P>I guess I am not down with that Vibe!||||reg||1
Z||000017||Galen||11-02-2001||02:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LZeitgeist:<BR><B> So why do you care?<P>Drive what you like... makes no difference to me. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I would respond, but ya know.. that would prolly make you feel special, & I dont wanna get your hopes up about that<P>------------------<BR><B>Ray</B> Webmaster of <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>Fierolinks</A><BR>"The price of love is tragedy"||||reg||1
